Easiest thing would be, as you say, to delete them before starting
every game. Easiest way to do *that* is to replace your nethack
startup icon/command for a script that deletes any and all bones files
present before starting the game up for you.

Alternatively, assuming your nethacking machine is connected to the
internet, get hearse. That gives you a multi-user-environment-like
bones pool. You can even set it to delete your own bones after
uploading them, so you only ever encounter other ppls' bones (except
in rare cases where someone downloads your bones, gets killed by them,
leaves more bones of the same level, and then uploads your own level
plus their grave for you to find again=-)

